Description: ComfyUI - node-based Stable Diffusion / generative AI UI
 The most powerful and modular visual AI engine and application. Design
 and execute image, video and audio generation pipelines as node graphs
 in the browser.
 .
 This package stages the upstream source tree, unmodified, under
 /usr/lib/comfyui and adds a "comfyui" launcher. Upstream distributes
 ComfyUI as a Python project installed with pip into a virtualenv, and
 its dependencies (PyTorch and friends, about 2.5 GB installed) are not in the
 Ubuntu archive, so the launcher creates that virtualenv per user in
 ~/.local/share/comfyui/venv on first run, installs the CPU build of
 PyTorch plus upstream's requirements.txt, and runs ComfyUI with that
 directory as its base for models, custom_nodes, input, output and user
 data. On Apple Silicon under Linux there is no GPU backend for PyTorch,
 so generation runs on the CPU and is slow.

